    "q-37685": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37685",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{y}^{1}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[x]_{y}^{1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}(1-y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{2})}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{1}^{2})}{2}-(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{0}^{2})}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
