      "dom_id": "step-q81197",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Calculate ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 2y}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 2y}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}({e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-y})\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}({e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-y})\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-y}[{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{e}^{x}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-y}[{e}^{x}]_{0}^{2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-y}({e}^{2y}-{e}^{0})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{y}-{e}^{-y})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{y}-{e}^{-y})\\,dy & =[{e}^{y}+{e}^{-y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({e}^{1}+{e}^{-1})-({e}^{0}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =e+\\frac{1}{e}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
