    "q-81292": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81292",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114695/assets/df3acf049579ec4de948d84d04d4fe3012c2232b9699d0471857227f52c78107.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $x={y}^{2},\\,$ $x=8-{y}^{2},$ and $y=0,$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dA=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. \n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-{y}^{2} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ 8 & =2{y}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114695/assets/2722224678aeb1f9ea64f42de2dc4fbf6e139350c291de16500957575fd23850.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 8-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{8-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{8-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81292-a",
